From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: sunshineinabox <aqemail@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 25 Nov 2026 12:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(GameLaunchMenu): give game settings its own copy of the
 launcher's data

The launch menu handed the game settings state the launcher state's own
data dictionary, and game settings erases "item" from its data when it
closes. Closing game settings so emptied the launcher's data: the
launcher, entered again right after, logged "No library item found to
configure launcher!" and returned before set_process(true), so its
button stopped following installs; and the next visit to game settings
had no game. Its title kept the last game's name only because
game_settings.gd keeps the item it had, but a plugin section that shows
only for its own games (RetroForge's per-game settings) was hidden until
the game was opened from the library again (MANGMI Air X, 2026-11-25).

Game settings now gets a copy, which it can erase from freely.
---
 core/ui/card_ui/launch/game_launch_menu.gd | 5 +++--
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/core/ui/card_ui/launch/game_launch_menu.gd b/core/ui/card_ui/launch/game_launch_menu.gd
index 6a59c81..e3b7e91 100644
--- a/core/ui/card_ui/launch/game_launch_menu.gd
+++ b/core/ui/card_ui/launch/game_launch_menu.gd
@@ -83,8 +83,9 @@ func _on_state_entered(_from: State) -> void:
 	logger.info("Configured launcher for game: " + library_item.name)
 	set_process(true)
 	
-	# Configure the game settings state with this game
-	game_settings_state.data = launcher_state.data
+	# Configure the game settings state with this game. A copy: game settings
+	# erases "item" from its data when it closes, which emptied this one too.
+	game_settings_state.data = launcher_state.data.duplicate()
 
 	# Configure the controller settings state with this game 
 	gamepad_settings_state.data = launcher_state.data ## DEPRECATED, use meta
